open_md='''Three confirmed blockers remain in frozen candidate-v13.0. These are HOST/SIMULATED findings; no native run or speed credit is claimed.\n\n1. **B01 — explicit fresh request ignored.** After full feedback, default `native --fresh` returns `feedback_complete`, `native_executed: false`, and zero collectors. `--final --fresh` does collect. Repro: `raw/default-path-v2--explicit-fresh-nonfinal.command.json`; repeated independently under `work/reproductions/initial-proof`.\n2. **B02 — incomplete original packet integrity.** Preserve the full original archive, change `native/manifest.json` to zero tests / no reset / foreign session, retain the original `result.json` digest, then ordinary `native --final` accepts with original reuse and no collector. Canonical `native.log` substitution and contradictory inner coverage also accept. Repro: `raw/tamper-manifest-mutation.json`, `raw/pristine-tamper-manifest.tar`, and `work/tamper-manifest/evidence/final-on-altered-packet/cycle.json`.\n3. **B03 — persisted cross-process monotonic epoch is unsafe on this host.** Python3.9.6 child clock starts before the parent’s pre-delay reading. Two compatible normal feedback captures retain the same pool key but produce two UUIDs/create intents within about 0.24 seconds under the default 300-second idle policy. Repro: `raw/host-monotonic-cross-process.json` and `raw/pool-consecutive-compatible-repro.json`. This demonstrates a HOST prerequisite and SIMULATED controller failure; real native pool reuse is U.\n\nI01 remains a protocol-interpretation dispute. The original omitted-separate-worker-CLI probe is F under a literal reading of H03, but the service actually emitted an automatic measured task-bound completion receipt and forced a new recheck. Missing/tampered proof controls reject. This is retained separately from the three confirmed blockers.\n\n`review.json` preserves all 47 primary raw outcomes (36 P / 11 F), including setup/probe limitations; the raw F count is not a bug count. Native PFU identity, resource deletion, full dependency closure and the >=20% AB/BA performance gate could not be evaluated.\n'''
(ROOT/'OPEN-ISSUES.md').write_text(open_md)

